# rootwhy — run a command with sudo after a password dialog that explains why and what it does.
# https://github.com/DragonKing026/rootwhy
"""rootwhy: sudo with a password dialog that shows the reason, the command split into coloured parts and
an explanation of every part on hover.

Two modes in one file:
  * main mode   — parses arguments, writes the log, runs `sudo -k -A -- command…` with this file as SUDO_ASKPASS;
  * askpass mode — started by sudo (ROOTWHY_MODE=askpass): shows the dialog, prints the password to stdout.
The password goes from the dialog straight to sudo; the caller (e.g. an AI agent) never sees it.
"""
